-- MULTI-VOXEL PATTERN ANALYSIS (MVPA)
-- Visualizes: Brain → fMRI Voxels → Pattern Extraction → Classifier
-- FILM-TITLE: "Multi-Voxel Pattern Analysis"
-- FILM: 0 5 "The Brain" "A living brain — billions of neurons firing. But we can't see individual neurons with fMRI. We see **blood oxygen levels** averaged over tiny cubes called **voxels**."
-- FILM: 5 11 "fMRI Scanning" "A scanner pulse sweeps through the brain. Each sweep captures a **3D snapshot** of activity — one number per voxel. The brain is now a grid of values, not tissue."
-- FILM: 11 17 "Stimulus → Activation" "Two stimuli are shown: a **face** and a **house**. Each triggers a different spatial pattern of voxel activity. The patterns overlap — no single voxel tells you which stimulus was shown."
-- FILM: 17 23 "Pattern Extraction" "MVPA reads the **entire pattern** across many voxels simultaneously. The face pattern (red) and house pattern (blue) are extracted as **feature vectors** — points in high-dimensional space."
-- FILM: 23 30 "Classifier Decodes" "A classifier (SVM/LDA) learns the **decision boundary** between patterns. Given a new brain scan, it reads the voxel pattern and predicts: **face or house?** The brain's code is cracked."
V 96 56 56
DUR 30
L 1

-- ============================================================
-- STAGE 1: THE BRAIN (T=0-5)
-- Two hemispheres, cerebellum, stem, with pulse
-- ============================================================

-- Left hemisphere
E 42*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) 28*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) 22*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) 16*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) 14*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) 12*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) b
-- Right hemisphere
E 54*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) 28*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) 22*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) 16*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) 14*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) 12*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) b

-- Hemisphere folds (cortex wrinkles — darker ridges)
E 42*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 34*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 22*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 14*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 4*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 10*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) e
E 54*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 34*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 22*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 14*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 4*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 10*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) e
E 42*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 28*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 13*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 12*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 10*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 3*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) e
E 54*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 28*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 13*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 12*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 10*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) 3*clamp(T*0.7,0,1) e

-- Central fissure (gap between hemispheres)
B 48*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) 28*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) 22*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) 1*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) 14*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) 12*clamp(T*0.8,0,1) e

-- Cerebellum (back-bottom)
E 48*clamp(T,0,1) 16*clamp(T,0,1) 32*clamp(T,0,1) 10*clamp(T,0,1) 6*clamp(T,0,1) 6*clamp(T,0,1) b

-- Brain stem
C 48*clamp(T,0,1) 6*clamp(T,0,1) 28*clamp(T,0,1) 3*clamp(T,0,1) 10*clamp(T,0,1) b

-- Alive pulse (subtle expanding glow)
S 48 28 22 14+bounce(T*2)*2 1

